config BR2_PACKAGE_PLEXOS_INIT
	bool "plexos-init"
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	help
	  MediaLith PID 1: sets up dm-verity over the /usr image, assembles
	  the root filesystem, and supervises services.

	  Built as a fully static binary, which is not a preference. The
	  initrd inside the Unified Kernel Image is this one file and
	  nothing else -- no dynamic loader, no libc, no modules
	  (ARCHITECTURE.md section 3). A dynamically linked build boots to
	  a panic naming a missing loader rather than the real cause.

	  Unlike every other package here, this one is compiled by the
	  workspace's own pinned Rust toolchain rather than by Buildroot.
	  Buildroot 2026.02 carries rustc 1.88 while rust-toolchain.toml
	  pins 1.94, and a static binary shares nothing with the target
	  toolchain anyway. The tradeoff is that an image build needs
	  cargo on the host; see package/plexos-init/plexos-init.mk.
